.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rosregview-help 1  "rosregview-help "
.SH NAME
rosregview\-help \- Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrosregview help\fR [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
rosregview\-help\-info(1)
Show a one\-line summary for a hive file: size, root subkey count
.TP
rosregview\-help\-tree(1)
Recursively print the key tree of a hive file (uses ASCII\-only indent)
.TP
rosregview\-help\-list(1)
List the direct subkeys of a key (default: the root), with subkey and value counts. The optional `KEY_PATH` may be a single segment (`ControlSet001`) or a backslash\-separated subpath (`A\\B\\C`). Empty path == the root
.TP
rosregview\-help\-show(1)
Show the values of a key (default: the root). Per\-value output includes the value name, its REG_* type, and the data, decoded according to the type where possible (UTF\-16 strings, u32 little\- endian dwords, u64 little\-endian qwords, ...). Binary data is shown as a hex dump; long strings are truncated with a trailing `…`
.TP
rosregview\-help\-find(1)
Search the key hierarchy for keys with names matching `\-n` (substring, repeatable, any\-of, case\-insensitive by default) and/or values whose name+decoded\-data contains `\-v`. With no filters, this enumerates every key path up to `\-\-max\-depth`
.TP
rosregview\-help\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
